# Live side-action UI safety

The backend owns eligibility, scoring, and payout math. The UI displays that contract safely.

## Scope and authorization

- Event lists require `action.event_id === eventId`; do not let missing IDs match every event.
- Hide event-scoped actions that cannot be used instead of showing controls that always fail.
- Gate every protected action, including details, standings, reports, edit, and delete.
- Do not infer authorization from role labels when capability hooks/data exist.

## Fresh server data

- Signup, roster, scoring, and configuration mutations invalidate affected list and standings keys.
- Reuse shared downstream invalidators instead of maintaining partial copies.
- Live standings use zero stale time plus polling or a visible refresh action when appropriate.
- API response types include completion, provisional, and overcommitment fields from the backend.
- Never calculate payable winnings in React.

## Display contracts

- Keep enum/storage value `HIGH_SET`; use one display helper for the label “High Series”.
- “All” reports use an aggregate title, never the first pot's name.
- Preserve and normalize legacy config shapes instead of silently broadening eligibility.
- Server-managed ticket types do not show misleading free-form quantity controls.
- Tables use `scope="col"` and repeated row actions include the pot name in `aria-label`.

Add tests for event filtering, permission gating, legacy config normalization, cache invalidation,
provisional payout messaging, and aggregate report naming.
